
1) We first samples (k+buffer) no. of samples, with maximum along those directions.
2) Use maximum of those samples as emperical f_max and do acceptance, rejection of those saved samples.
3) Now you still need remaining(=k-accepted_in_step-2) samples. Now samples (remaining+buffer) no. samples with
   maximums in those directions.
4) - Get emperical f_max of this new batch, if it is less than < old_f_max then we use old_f_max for acceptance of new sample 
     and add new accepted samples in the already accepted samples list.
   - If new emperical f_max > old_f_max then now we will have to modify the old accepted samples as well. 
     we go through all previous accepteed sample and check acceptance with this new emperical f_max, and same with 
     new accepted samples. 
5) we repeat step 3,4 till we have k no. of accepted samples.


